# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ClipDock - what is deliberately NOT in the repository.
#
# Three of the four large folders here are generated, and all three are
# reproducible from a clean checkout by running scripts\setup.ps1 and then
# scripts\build_installer.ps1.  Keeping them out of git is not only about size:
# a committed .venv or vendor\ folder goes stale against requirements.txt, and
# nothing then tells you which of the two the tests actually ran against.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python bytecode -------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# --- Virtual environment ---------------------------------------------------
# Recreated by scripts\setup.ps1, which also fetches and checksum-verifies the
# pinned dependencies below.
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python

# --- Dependencies fetched at setup time ------------------------------------
# ~145 MB of FFmpeg.  tools\fetch_dependencies.py verifies it against the
# SHA-256 pins in tools\fetch_dependencies.py itself, so an absent folder is
# rebuilt and verified rather than trusted.
vendor/

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# dist\ClipDock\        the PyInstaller folder build_exe.ps1 produces
# dist\ClipDock-Setup.exe  the installer, ~47 MB
#
# Neither belongs in version control.  dist\ClipDock-Setup.exe is a release
# artefact: attach it to a GitHub Release instead of committing it, so the tag
# and the file that was tagged stay in agreement.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- PyInstaller -----------------------------------------------------------
# Written beside the sources during a build; regenerated every time.
*.spec

# --- Test, lint and coverage output ----------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Icon generator output -------------------------------------------------
# tools\make_icon.py renders every size it needs to disk next to the .ico.
#
# assets\app.ico IS committed and the glob below deliberately excludes it: the
# program loads that file at runtime, build_exe.ps1 packs it, and a test
# requires it to be byte-identical to what the generator produces today, so it
# must never drift out of the repository.  The PNGs are intermediate renders
# that nothing reads, which is exactly why they are the ones ignored.
assets/app-*.png

# --- Runtime output, wherever the program happens to run --------------------
*.log
logs/
settings.json

# --- Editor and operating-system noise -------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej